===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|مُحَمَّد||[[praise]]d, [[commendable]], [[laudable]]}}, the passive participle of {{m|ar|حَمَّدَ||to [[praise]], [[commend]], [[laud]], [[extol]]}}. From the same triconsonantal root {{ar-root|ح|م|د}} as, but distinct from, {{term|Mahmud|lang=en}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The [[figure]] who [[introduce]]d [[Islam]], the man to whom the [[Quran]] was [[reveal]]ed; considered a prophet by Muslims and [[Baha'i]]s.
#: ''Shias believe that Ali succeeded the prophet '''Muhammad''' as leader of the Ummah.''
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The 47th [[sura]] (chapter) of the [[Quran]].
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} very popular among [[Muslim]]s.
#: ''There are two '''Muhammads''' in my class.''

